  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent negative bias: model underprices the level by ~2–6 EUR across most horizons; apply an upward level shift, larger when the recent trend is up.",
    "Trend/lag error: in rising regimes the forecast path reacts too slowly (lags the upswing). Add a positive trend term proportional to the last 5–10 day slope, especially for days 5–25 ahead.",
    "Underestimation increases with horizon: errors grow from small at day 1–3 to large by day 10–30. Use a horizon-dependent uplift (e.g., +1–2 EUR near-term, scaling to +4–6 EUR by day 20–30 in bullish regimes).",
    "Excess mean-reversion: model pulls prices back toward ~63–66 too aggressively, while outcomes stay elevated (~67–70). Reduce mean-reversion strength when price breaks above recent 20–30d range highs.",
    "Post-spike behavior: after upward breaks, model tends to fade/flatten; instead, enforce momentum persistence (keep forecasts elevated) for ~2–3 weeks following a breakout."
  ]
